From 858f4438d77738cc43e3e302e84f8e614daa23c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel <2660793+imDaniel@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 12:02:29 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Isolate Attention prefix hashes from caller salts at engine
 admission

Base: qualified downstream vLLM 9a71ded060b015e40f721a9caf506e43bd1f3fa0 with the independent tool-encoding fix applied first.

Keep the wire salt as supplied. Load the pinned Attention profile in the core and derive a tagged first-block key before scheduling, including prebuilt EngineCoreRequests. The parent hash carries this dimension through subsequent blocks. Preserve stock, zero scale, explicit caller salts, and the existing GLP key.

Quality: isolates KV produced by different projected writers without changing logits, profile contents or accepted strengths. Existing active hashes change namespace; the eligible site configuration uses process-local prefix caches.

Tests: steering request and profile CPU contracts plus real EngineCoreRequest preprocessing and two-block hash chains for normal and prebuilt requests with SHA-256 pickle and CBOR.

Upstream status: downstream Attention maintenance.
